lisa-design:
Round 3 (design §13.4, R74-R79) and the origin/main merge (#96/#97):
- Merge: policy sources stay keyed by filepath.Clean(path given to the plugin), the same key WithPolicyPaths uses; an inline bundle's key is its stable <state>/inline/<b>/current/bundle path. Inline sources are runner.Source{Reference: "inline:<b>", Digest: tree digest, BundleArtifact: true}: evidence records the stored bundle's artifact digest (refs.BundleDigest) and falls back to the tree digest only when the bundle could not be stored. The extends source stays on the report, never on evidence.
- R74: policy-manager seeds through policyeval.SeedPath only when Result.Policy.ID is set, overriding _policy_path in the SEED map only when the plugin labels it; without an ID evidenceSeed is MergeMaps(base, p.labels) exactly as before (golden UUIDs pinned). _policy_id is set last in labels (authoritative over plugin/result labels). Risk template UUIDs are unchanged (still policy_file based): out of scope.
- Known limit (needs an API change, not agent): a local source configured non-clean (./policies) cannot be continued for plugins that label _policy_path: legacy seed is (clean file, literal "./policies"), and SeedPath returns either (id, clean prefix) or (unclean id, literal prefix). Fix would be SeedPath returning path.Clean(id) as the file seed + UI writing the literal <plugin-path>/<file>.
- R75: identity checks run per plugin that uses an inline bundle (vendor-only plugins are the file's business), over every module of every path. Static policy_id = the API contract's accepted form only (single `policy_id := "<literal>"` per package). Severity of duplicate-policy-id/-identity: error when the overlay touches /plugins/<p>/policies or /policy_bundles/<b> of a bundle involved, else warning (R34) - deliberate deviation from "always error" for duplicate-policy-id from the file. Same-entry duplicate ids are skipped when both or neither are authored (API CheckContract / vendor debt). Continuity is compared by seeds (inlinepolicy.SeedOf), not by string-matching a policy_id, so it tracks SeedPath exactly.
- policy-stream-forked is an agent-local code (no API constant yet); the UI should label it. policy-package-changed uses the API constant.
- R76/R79: the gate runs after Prefetch (binaries are local then), reads build info via debug/buildinfo (pluginlib.Cache keyed by path+size+mtime), and is skipped entirely when rc.pluginLib is nil (tests). MinInlinePolicy = v0.9.0 (pre-releases count; v0.8.0 is being cut without R74); pseudo-versions compare by their base tag; replace/(devel)/no build info/untagged pseudo => unknown => warnings only. Overlay-introduced + unsupported => error plugin-lib-inline-unsupported per bundle, plus a located plugin-lib-violation-set-unsupported when lib < v0.7.1. File-origin => warnings, plus per-module plugin-lib-policy-id-unsupported (superseded by the gate for overlay bundles). Policy rejections from the gate never set aerr.runtime (that would fire the startup-failure evidence hook).
- R77: PluginPath = m.Path for inline, resolver output for OCI/local (the same string runPluginWith/DownloadPolicies pass).
